ssh and gpg keys in githubs
uses public key cryptography

public/private keys:
a method for securely passing data from one place to another
provides a very high level of confidence that the data is coming from the place it claims to be coming from

SSH Key — for connecting to GitHub
An SSH key lets your computer authenticate with GitHub without entering your GitHub password/token every time.
git push, git pull, git clone authentication

GPG Key — for signing commits
A GPG key is mainly used to prove that a commit was genuinely created/signed by you.